{"units": [{"id": "basileios-quote1", "translation": "and about the royal return."}, {"id": "basileios-quote2", "translation": "the city-destroying royal army."}, {"id": "basileios-quote3", "translation": "for the royal power has utterly perished."}, {"id": "basileios-quote4", "translation": "of the royal tiara."}, {"id": "basileios-quote5", "translation": "with a royal offering from the inner shrine."}, {"id": "basileios-quote6", "translation": "in royal houses."}, {"id": "basileios-quote7", "translation": "in royal halls."}, {"id": "basileios-quote8", "translation": "with the body – the royal one."}, {"id": "basileios-quote9", "translation": "in the royal halls."}, {"id": "basileios-quote10", "translation": "royal sufferings."}, {"id": "basileios-quote11", "translation": "the forerunner of the royal halls."}, {"id": "basileus-orth1", "translation": "king"}, {"id": "basileus-def1", "translation": "king"}, {"id": "basileus-note1", "translation": "(eagle)"}, {"id": "basileus-quote1", "translation": "lord Xerxes the king."}, {"id": "basileus-quote2", "translation": "Xerxes the king."}, {"id": "basileus-quote3", "translation": "blessed king equal to the gods."}, {"id": "basileus-quote4", "translation": "king Darius equal to a god."}, {"id": "basileus-quote5", "translation": "king of birds"}, {"id": "basileus-quote6", "translation": "for he was king:"}, {"id": "basileus-quote7", "translation": "under the dread escort of the king."}, {"id": "basileus-quote8", "translation": "mother of the king."}, {"id": "basileus-quote9", "translation": "subject to the king."}, {"id": "basileus-quote10", "translation": "with the king's lamentation."}, {"id": "basileus-quote11", "translation": "receive the king with honor."}, {"id": "basileus-quote12", "translation": "O Zeus the king."}, {"id": "basileus-quote13", "translation": "O Zeus the king."}, {"id": "basileus-quote14", "translation": "and king of those below."}, {"id": "basileus-quote15", "translation": "Alas, O king."}, {"id": "basileus-quote16", "translation": "king of the land."}, {"id": "basileus-quote17", "translation": "come now, O king."}, {"id": "basileus-quote18", "translation": "O king, O king."}, {"id": "basileus-quote19", "translation": "O king, O king."}, {"id": "basileus-quote20", "translation": "and of the two kings of the same seed."}, {"id": "basileus-quote21", "translation": "kings subject to the great king."}, {"id": "basileus-quote22", "translation": "kings, stewards."}, {"id": "basileus-quote23", "translation": "halls of kings."}, {"id": "basileus-quote24", "translation": "quarrels of kings."}, {"id": "basileus-quote25", "translation": "with kings."}, {"id": "basileus-quote26", "translation": "to the kings of ships."}, {"id": "basilikos-orth1", "translation": "royal"}, {"id": "basilikos-def1", "translation": "royal"}, {"id": "basilikos-quote1", "translation": "she will bear a royal race in Argos."}, {"id": "basis-orth1", "translation": "step"}, {"id": "basis-def1", "translation": "step. Improperly"}, {"id": "basis-note1", "translation": "where the scholiast says: ἠρεμαίᾳ τῇ ψυχῇ [with a calm soul], ἀντὶ τοῦ προσέχων καὶ μὴ ἀποπλανώμενος [instead of paying attention and not wandering]."}, {"id": "basis-quote1", "translation": "with a quiet step of the mind,"}, {"id": "basis-word1", "translation": "with a calm soul, instead of paying attention and not wandering"}, {"id": "baskō-orth1", "translation": "to go"}, {"id": "baskō-def1", "translation": "same as βαίνω [to go], to walk, to come"}, {"id": "baskō-quote1", "translation": "go, gentle father."}, {"id": "baskō-word1", "translation": "to go"}, {"id": "bassarai-orth1", "translation": "Bassarae"}, {"id": "bassarai-def1", "translation": "Bassarae, Thracian bacchae,"}, {"id": "bassarai-note1", "translation": "about which see what has been collected in the Thesaurus vol. 2 p. 180-182. Thus was titled the second play of Aeschylus' Lycurgeia tetralogy (fr. 20-22b), not Βασσαρίδες [Bassarides], as is read in some places of the grammarians, about which I have spoken in my note on the Fragments p. 101."}, {"id": "bassarai-word1", "translation": "Bassarides"}, {"id": "bastazō-orth1", "translation": "to carry"}, {"id": "bastazō-def1", "translation": "to carry"}, {"id": "bastazō-def2", "translation": "to handle"}, {"id": "bastazō-note1", "translation": "Blomfield collected other examples."}, {"id": "bastazō-quote1", "translation": "who first carried this in his mind."}, {"id": "bastazō-quote2", "translation": "and a rocky embrace will carry you."}, {"id": "bastazō-quote3", "translation": "I will carry the dear hand of the lord of the house with this hand."}, {"id": "batanōchos-orth1", "translation": "Batanōchos"}, {"id": "batanōchos-def1", "translation": "Persian proper name"}, {"id": "bauzō-orth1", "translation": "to cry out"}, {"id": "bauzō-def1", "translation": "to cry out"}, {"id": "bauzō-note1", "translation": "i.e. demands with a loud cry. Hesychius explains it as ἀσαφῶς λέγειν [to speak unclearly]."}, {"id": "bauzō-quote1", "translation": "and cries out for a young man,"}, {"id": "bauzō-quote2", "translation": "someone cries out these things in silence."}, {"id": "bauzō-word1", "translation": "to speak unclearly"}, {"id": "baphē-orth1", "translation": "dye"}, {"id": "baphē-def1", "translation": "dye"}, {"id": "baphē-quote1", "translation": "changing his skin with purple dye."}, {"id": "baphē-quote2", "translation": "pouring the dye of saffron to the ground."}, {"id": "baphē-quote3", "translation": "I know no pleasure or blameworthy report from another man more than the dipping of bronze."}, {"id": "baphē-quote4", "translation": "dyeings of garments."}, {"id": "baphē-quote5", "translation": "destroying many dyes of the embroidery."}, {"id": "bdelyktropos-orth1", "translation": "abominable"}, {"id": "bdelyktropos-def1", "translation": "abominable"}, {"id": "bdelyktropos-note1", "translation": "On the form of this adjective see Lobeck on Phrynichus p. 671."}, {"id": "bdelyktropos-quote1", "translation": "utterly abominable."}, {"id": "bebaios-orth1", "translation": "firm, certain"}, {"id": "bebaios-def1", "translation": "firm, certain"}, {"id": "bebaios-quote1", "translation": "neither of flowery spring nor of fruitful summer is there a sure (sign)."}, {"id": "bebaios-quote2", "translation": "and remedies not sure."}, {"id": "bebaios-quote3", "translation": "for you will never say that the friend of Oceanus is more steadfast to you."}, {"id": "bebaiōs-orth1", "translation": "firmly"}, {"id": "bebaiōs-def1", "translation": "firmly"}, {"id": "bebaiōs-quote1", "translation": "not to close the eyelids firmly in sleep."}, {"id": "bebēlos-orth1", "translation": "profane"}, {"id": "bebēlos-def1", "translation": "profane"}, {"id": "bebēlos-quote1", "translation": "and how could a profane grove protect me?"}, {"id": "belemnon-orth1", "translation": "missile"}, {"id": "belemnon-def1", "translation": "missile"}, {"id": "belemnon-quote1", "translation": "with a double-edged missile."}, {"id": "belos-orth1", "translation": "missile"}, {"id": "belos-def1", "translation": "missile"}, {"id": "belos-def2", "translation": "The figurative use of the word is manifold. Of the thunderbolt"}, {"id": "belos-def3", "translation": "Of the sting of the gadfly and scorpion"}, {"id": "belos-def4", "translation": "of the sting of love, pity"}, {"id": "belos-def5", "translation": "of words"}, {"id": "belos-def6", "translation": "of a storm"}, {"id": "belos-note1", "translation": "(ξίφη [swords] from the scholiast, Pauw.)"}, {"id": "belos-quote1", "translation": "so that neither before the time nor beyond the stars may a vain missile fall."}, {"id": "belos-quote2", "translation": "I was struck as by a piercing missile."}]}